========================================================================================================================
HPE VM ESSENTIALS (VME) 8.1.2 - VM MIGRATION TROUBLESHOOTING & RECOVERY
========================================================================================================================

CATEGORY               COMMAND                                         DESCRIPTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Migration Monitoring   sudo virsh jobinfo <domain>                     Check progress, speed, & remaining memory of live migration
Migration Monitoring   sudo virsh list --all                           Run on source and target to verify where the VM is stuck
Migration Monitoring   sudo pcs resource status                        Verify if Pacemaker recognizes the VM resource relocation
Migration Monitoring   sudo virsh domjobabort <domain>                 Forcefully cancel a hung or frozen live migration job

Manual Relocation      sudo virsh migrate --live <domain> qemu+ssh://<target_node_ip>/system
                                                                       Force a manual libvirt live migration via SSH tunnel
Manual Relocation      sudo pcs resource move <vm_resource_id> <node>   Gracefully instruct Pacemaker to migrate VM to specific node
Manual Relocation      sudo pcs resource clear <vm_resource_id>        Remove the explicit location constraint created by 'move'

Network & Pre-flight   ping -s 8972 <target_migration_ip>               Test Jumbo Frames (MTU 9000) stability between cluster nodes
Network & Pre-flight   nc -zv <target_node_ip> 49152-49215             Scan if QEMU dynamic live migration port range is open
Network & Pre-flight   sudo virsh capabilities | grep exact             Verify CPU model flags match exactly between source & target

Migration Log Analysis tail -f /var/log/libvirt/libvirtd.log          Monitor underlying virtualization API migration errors
Migration Log Analysis tail -f /var/log/libvirt/qemu/<domain>.log      Stream VM-specific engine logs (identifies QEMU drops)
Migration Log Analysis grep -i "migration" /var/log/pacemaker/pacemaker.log
                                                                       Search cluster manager for failed transition steps
Migration Log Analysis grep -iE "timeout|abort" /var/log/libvirt/libvirtd.log
                                                                       Isolate memory dirty-rate timeouts during live sync
